WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.560
MARK MOORE: The world in which
each of us, and all of us,

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.660
now live is full of pressing
problems and future risks.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.070
But it's also full of hope,
aspiration, and opportunity.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.920
Public leaders can come
in many different guises.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.400
They can be ordinary citizens
who take up a local cause.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.450
They can manage a non-profit
organization or a voluntary association

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.540
that provides services to
those in need and security

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.370
to those who are oppressed.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.400
They can be individuals who
run for elective office,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.900
hoping to create more economic,
social, or political equality.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.390
They can serve in government,
hoping to increase

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.070
the responsiveness,
efficiency, effectiveness,

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.710
and fairness of government operations.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.710
In Leadership, Creating
Public Value, you

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:52.910
will learn how to face and meet the
challenge of diagnosing the reality you

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.270
confront and designing a
public value proposition that

00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:00.140
is both plausibly value-creating
and actionable by you

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.150
in your particular context.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.790
Through case studies, you
will see real public leaders

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.340
seeking to challenge the status quo.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.100
You'll be asked to reflect
on their thought and action,

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.310
using the analytic frameworks and
concepts developed and applied

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.360
throughout the course.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.570
The goal is simple.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.900
Learn how to create
long-term public value

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.240
by envisioning and enacting a better
and more just future for us all.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.759
[MUSIC PLAYING]

